// Ch12 camp (optional, the Quellan inn, the night after Cloudloom; requires ch12_ysolde_confessed). Toma and Ysolde,
// two people of the Order. Ysolde has read Ama Quillo's count; Toma does the sum to its end, and the end is Asha. He was
// made to keep her safe to the end of the road; nobody told him what was there (pillar 6). No Act III fact: nobody says
// what the Hush does (that is Ch16's). Sets ch12_camp_talk.
title: ch12_camp_the_end_of_the_road
location: ch12/quellan
---
Toma [neutral]: Forty-seven knots. #line:ch12_camp_001
Ysolde [neutral]: Forty-seven Cantors, up to Ama Quillo's own name. And the ones since. #line:ch12_camp_002
Toma [neutral]: And then the Lady Cantor's mother. #line:ch12_camp_003
Ysolde [sad]: Yes. #line:ch12_camp_004
Toma [neutral]: And then her. #line:ch12_camp_005
Ysolde [neutral]: The cords do not say that. #line:ch12_camp_006
Toma [cold]: They do not need to. #line:ch12_camp_007
Toma [neutral]: When I took the oath, they said, keep her safe to the end of the road. I said I would. I meant it. #line:ch12_camp_008
Toma [grief]: Nobody told me what was at the end of it. #line:ch12_camp_009
Ysolde [guilty]: I knew more than you did. Not all of it. More. #line:ch12_camp_010
-> Toma: "Why didn't you say?" #line:ch12_camp_011
    Ysolde [guilty]: Because I wanted it to be wrong. And because I am a coward about the things I love. #line:ch12_camp_012
-> Toma: "Will you tell me now?" #line:ch12_camp_013
    Ysolde [neutral]: Everything I learn. The day I learn it. I promise you that. #line:ch12_camp_014
Toma [neutral]: Then I will keep her safe to the end of the road. And then I will see what the road is. #line:ch12_camp_015
<<set $ch12_camp_talk = true>>
===
